<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Dexterity</h1>
<p>Dexterity (DEX) is one of your abilities: how quick and nimble you are. It 
determines:
</p>
<ul><li><b>Your defence in a fight.</b> The nimbler you are, the more blows you dodge.</li>
<li><b>Your attack with weapons.</b> Each weapon draws on two of your abilities: nearly all on two parts strength to one part dexterity, but the whip, the sickle and the bow, crossbow and sling on two parts dexterity (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>).</li>
<li><b>How many things you can carry</b>: ten items, and one more for every ten points of dexterity.</li>
<li><b>Many skills</b>: backstab, climbing, sneaking, hiding, stealing, picking locks and others compare your dexterity with your target's or with the task.</li></ul>
<p>Heavy armour slows you down: chain and above all plate lower your dexterity 
in a fight, unless you are strong and well practiced in that armour (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Armour</a>). The spell dexterity raises it for a while.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
